+/*
+ * Copyright 2026, haiku-odroid-c2 port authors.
+ * Distributed under the terms of the MIT License.
+ *
+ * meson_mali: the ODROID-C2's Mali-450 MP3 GPU, for Mesa's lima driver
+ * (PLAN.md M43). This is stage 2, the bring-up: the clock, the GPU's own
+ * power management unit, the version registers, the two L2 caches, the
+ * geometry processor's (GP) and pixel processors' (PP) soft resets, the four
+ * MMUs on an empty address space (the load balancer's page mapped at its
+ * fixed address), the load balancer (DLBU) and broadcast units, and the ten
+ * interrupts, checked with the reset-completed interrupts. Jobs and lima's
+ * interface come in stage 3.
+ *
+ * The facts are in the port's docs/m43-mali-facts.md (the GPU) and
+ * docs/m43-gxbb-mali-integration-facts.md (its clock and interrupts on the
+ * S905). On the GXBB the GPU has no reset line or power domain of its own
+ * that Linux uses: the clock is all, and the GPU's PMU powers its parts.
+ */
+
+
